\pard\b\f0\fs24 Tex Kovachnikov\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Ethnicity:\b0\f1  American Russian.\par
\b\f0 Position:\b0\f1  Mechanic and heavy weapons specialist.\par
\b\f0 Age:\b0\f1  36.\par
\b\f0 Sex:\b0\f1  Male.\par
\b\f0 Height:\b0\f1  190 cm.\par
\b\f0 Build:\b0\f1  Muscular.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  John's enforcer, mechanic and blunt moral weather-vane. Tex often says what the rest of the squad are only thinking and absorbs the ugliest parts of the mission.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Protect his people, hit hard when diplomacy fails, and keep faith with the few people he truly trusts.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  Huge shoulders, thick frame and the presence of a brawler. He looks intimidating, but there is warmth beneath the bulk.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Rough, funny, fiercely loyal and smarter than he pretends. He masks grief and political anger behind crude humour and bravado.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Protectant mechanic, field repairman and occasional rail gunner.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Jokes under pressure. Plays down his intelligence. Treats violence as honest language when trust breaks down.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Sole survivor of an asteroid strike that took his family. The loss left him hostile toward political complacency and suspicious of technocratic authority.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  Carries old grief, resentment and a trained instinct toward violence that later has to be re-aligned before safe {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://810E6D32-0F7D-4F6E-BAEE-0CE733205F8D"}{\fldrsltgate}} transit.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Repeatedly clashes with Marcellus's methods and is physically maimed saving the team before undergoing regrowth and alignment.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  Tex's later empathy training is one of the clearest examples of Serva Vitae trying to heal trauma instead of merely weaponising strength.\par
}
